          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "explanation": "It wins almost every major engagement. It is the war it cannot win: the enemy replaces its losses and comes back."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Washington measures progress by counting enemy dead. But the North accepts far heavier losses than the United States does. Ho Chi Minh had warned the French twenty years earlier."
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "You will kill ten of us, we will kill one of you, and it is you who will tire of it first.",
          "attribution": "Ho Chi Minh, 1946"
        }
      ]
    },
